<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Ms. O&apos;Keeffe is seen in the retina clinic two days after her primary care visit, where new distortion and a blurred central spot in the left eye were found on the Amsler grid. Over the past few weeks straight lines on her canvases and door frames have looked bent with the left eye, and small print and fine color differences have become hard to judge. The right eye seems unchanged. She has had no eye pain, redness, flashes, or new floaters. She takes no blood thinners and no other medicines. She paints daily and is afraid of losing the central vision she needs for her work. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Onset</td><td>Over the past few weeks</td></tr><tr><td>Symptoms</td><td>Bent lines and a central blurred spot, left eye; trouble with small print and fine color differences</td></tr><tr><td>Fellow eye</td><td>No change noticed in the right eye</td></tr><tr><td>Pertinent negatives</td><td>No pain, redness, flashes, or new floaters</td></tr><tr><td>Medicines</td><td>None; no anticoagulants</td></tr><tr><td>Patient concern</td><td>Keeping the central vision she needs to paint</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

